# SABOTAGE: T160 (spec §I4 completion, operator ruling 2026-08-06) — drops the org-pin
# filter (`org_id == ^config.org_id`) from `Samen.CRM.AccountLink.domain_match/2`'s
# candidate read (the fail-closed vaulted-domain-match fallback). Without it, the
# candidate scan runs across EVERY org's billing customers, so a CRM Company whose
# `domain` happens to match some OTHER org's billing customer's email domain resolves
# to that FOREIGN customer's real MRR/subscription-status — the exact T74 cross-tenant
# lesson (`Samen.Mailbox.Match.candidate_people/1`'s own org pin) reopened at the
# billing-linkage seam. `authorize?: false` here is a TRUSTED-config-pin read (the org
# boundary is meant to come from the caller's own scope, never from row data) — dropping
# the filter turns that trust into an unbounded, unscoped scan. Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_account_health_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: T160 FAIL-CLOSED NO-CROSS-ORG (the T74 lesson): a company's domain matches a DIFFERENT org's billing customer -> NEVER links across orgs
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
@@ -155,7 +155,6 @@
       config.customer_resource
       |> Ash.Query.new()
       |> Ash.Query.ensure_selected([:billing_email])
-      |> Ash.Query.filter(org_id == ^config.org_id)
       |> Ash.Query.limit(config.max_match_candidates)
       |> Ash.read!(authorize?: false)
       |> PiiResolution.resolve(config.customer_resource, %{plane: :tenant}, repo: config.repo)
